SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC : environ 124 cas d’atteintes à la liberté de la presse recensés en 10 mois","publisher":"Radio Okapi","publication_date":"2022-11-02","url":"https://www.radiookapi.net/2022/11/02/actualite/societe/rdc-environ-124-cas-datteintes-la-liberte-de-la-presse-recenses-en-10","claim":"JED said it recorded about 124 press-freedom violations in the DRC between January and October 2022, including 37 arrests, 18 assaults, 2 kidnappings, 1 killing, and 17 bans on media or programs.","locator":"lines 150-153","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Local reporting on a national watchdog's annual tally with concrete counts and a dated 2022 period.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong: the violations describe the media environment under Tshisekedi's administration.","contrary_evidence":["The tally aggregates abuses by multiple perpetrators, so not every violation is directly presidentially ordered."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.6","4B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Elections in the Era of Tshisekedi: A bad start?","publisher":"Center on International Cooperation, New York University","publication_date":"2022-10-18","url":"https://cic.nyu.edu/resources/elections-in-the-era-of-tshisekedi-a-bad-start/","claim":"The report says that with 14 months left before the next elections, the electoral calendar was still pending, distrust in CENI remained, and controversial reappointments to the Constitutional Court reinforced the lack of trust; it also says political control persisted over CENI and the Constitutional Court.","locator":"lines 83-91","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Research report from a Congo-focused academic center, directly discussing electoral institutions and published in the target year.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year and about the next electoral cycle under Tshisekedi.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong institutional attribution to Tshisekedi's era and the electoral bodies operating under his administration.","contrary_evidence":["The report is an analytic assessment, not direct proof of a presidential order."],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.2","4B.4","4B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC : GEC et Ebuteli alertent sur « un spectre de glissement du calendrier électoral »","publisher":"Radio Okapi","publication_date":"2022-10-19","url":"https://www.radiookapi.net/2022/10/19/actualite/politique/rdc-gec-et-ebuteli-alertent-sur-un-spectre-de-glissement-du","claim":"Radio Okapi reports that GEC and Ebuteli warned that the electoral calendar was still pending, that trust in CENI remained weak, and that political control persisted over CENI and the Constitutional Court, raising a risk of slippage beyond constitutional deadlines.","locator":"lines 150-159","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Local coverage of a Congo-focused research report with explicit quotes and direct 2022 timing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant to Tshisekedi because the critique targets the electoral institutions shaping his succession environment.","contrary_evidence":["This is a warning about process risk, not proof that deadlines were actually missed in 2022."],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.2","4B.4","4B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC : La CENI publie le calendrier électoral du cycle 2022-2027","publisher":"Radio Okapi","publication_date":"2022-11-26","url":"https://www.radiookapi.net/2022/11/26/actualite/politique/rdc-la-ceni-publie-le-calendrier-electoral-du-cycle-2022-2027","claim":"CENI published the 2022-2027 electoral calendar on 26 November 2022, setting presidential, legislative, provincial, and communal elections for 20 December 2023 and saying that slippage was not in its vocabulary.","locator":"lines 156-160","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct reporting on the election body's public timetable and a concrete quotation about respecting the schedule.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year and directly relevant to the next electoral cycle.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant because the timetable was set under Tshisekedi's administration and his government publicly backed it.","contrary_evidence":["This records a plan and pledge, not verified completion of a free contest or transfer."],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Congo voter registration marred by early kit shortages","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-12-26","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/12/26/congo-election","claim":"Reuters reported that the opening of voter registration was marred by long lines, undersupplied stations, lack of staff and material, and shortages of registration kits, with only 6,900 of more than 11,000 kits delivered for the first phase.","locator":"lines 669-677","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters dispatch with specific observations, quantities, and contemporaneous reporting from the opening of registration.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly at the end of the target year and at the start of the election cycle.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant to Tshisekedi's administration because it concerns the state-run election process he was expected to inherit into his reelection bid.","contrary_evidence":["The article frames the problem as logistical and resource-related as well as political."],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.2","4B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Le Président Félix Tshisekedi pour la mise en œuvre des instruments juridiques portant protection des droits des PVH","publisher":"Agence Congolaise de Presse","publication_date":"2022-07-22","url":"https://acp.cd/nation/le-president-felix-tshisekedi-pour-la-mise-en-oeuvre-des-instruments-juridiques-portant-protection-des-droits-des-pvh/","claim":"ACP reports that Tshisekedi, in a 15 July 2022 Council of Ministers communication, praised the new disability law, called it the first such framework in the DRC, and ordered the government to prepare a timetable to make it effective.","locator":"lines 169-172","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government source quoting the president's own communication, with concrete implementation instructions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Tshisekedi as the president issuing the instruction and framing the reform.","contrary_evidence":["The source shows a directive and implementation plan, not proof of full execution in 2022."],"lenses":["4B.4","4B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"CENCO-ECC : Planification d’une mission d'observation électorale citoyenne","publisher":"Agence Congolaise de Presse","publication_date":"2022-10-17","url":"https://acp.cd/nation/cenco-ecc-planification-dune-mission-dobservation-electorale-citoyenne/","claim":"ACP says CENCO and ECC planned a citizen election-observation mission, asked CENI for accreditation of nearly 600 observers, and CENI gave them election maps, the law, application measures, and voter-registration documents.","locator":"lines 173-178","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary local report on a concrete interaction between civil-society observers and the election body.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant to Tshisekedi because it reflects how open the electoral process was to independent monitoring under his administration.","contrary_evidence":["This shows procedural access, not that the process itself was fully fair."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.4"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Le Président Félix Tshisekedi pour la mise en œuvre des instruments juridiques portant protection des droits des PVH","publisher":"Agence Congolaise de Presse","publication_date":"2022-07-22","url":"https://acp.cd/nation/le-president-felix-tshisekedi-pour-la-mise-en-oeuvre-des-instruments-juridiques-portant-protection-des-droits-des-pvh/","claim":"ACP reports that Tshisekedi called for implementing the new disability-rights law and that the government was tasked with producing a work timetable and related structural measures by the next cabinet meeting.","locator":"lines 169-171","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government report with direct presidential communication and a specific implementation order.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Tshisekedi's formal direction to the government.","contrary_evidence":["The article is about implementation planning, not demonstrated outcomes for disabled citizens in 2022."],"lenses":["4B.4","4B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Fonction publique : J-P Lihau signe l'arrêté portant création du Secrétariat général du ministère des Personnes vivant avec handicap","publisher":"Actu30","publication_date":"2022-11-22","url":"https://actu30.cd/2022/11/fonction-publique-j-p-lihau-signe-larrete-portant-creation-du-secretariat-general-du-ministere-des-personnes-vivant-avec-handicap/","claim":"Actu30 reports that the government created a dedicated secretariat-general for the ministry for persons living with disabilities, and officials described it as the materialization of Tshisekedi's inclusion vision.","locator":"lines 76-85","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous local reporting on an administrative reform tied to the presidency and disability inclusion.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Tshisekedi's political vision and the government's implementation of that vision.","contrary_evidence":["The reform is administrative and symbolic as well as substantive, so it does not by itself prove broader equality outcomes."],"lenses":["4B.4","4B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Reconnaissance des droits des peuples autochtones pygmées : une victoire historique en RDC","publisher":"Agir ensemble pour les droits humains","publication_date":"2022-12-01","url":"https://agir-ensemble-droits-humains.org/fr/communique-rdc-reconnaissance-des-droits-des-peuples-autochtones-pygmees-une-victoire-historique-en-rdc/","claim":"The organization says the law protecting and promoting indigenous Pygmy rights was passed by Parliament on 11 June 2022, sent to President Tshisekedi, promulgated on 15 July 2022, and published on 14 November 2022.","locator":"lines 12-13","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Rights-organization statement with exact dates for parliamentary passage, presidential promulgation, and publication.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Tshisekedi because the source states he promulgated the law.","contrary_evidence":["The source emphasizes a long advocacy process, so the reform was overdue rather than a newly initiated opening."],"lenses":["4B.7","4B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Réforme de la justice : près de 80 hauts magistrats ont prêté serment devant le Président de la République","publisher":"Présidence de la République Démocratique du Congo","publication_date":"2022-08-31","url":"https://presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/reforme_de_la_justice_pres_de_80_hauts_magistrats_ont_prete_serment_devant_le_president_de_la_republique","claim":"The presidential office says nearly 80 senior magistrates of the ordinary and administrative judiciary swore their oath before Tshisekedi on 31 August 2022, and it framed the ceremony as part of his effort to continue reforms and consolidate the rule of law.","locator":"lines 74-87","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential record of a formal judicial reform ceremony, though naturally self-presenting.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Tshisekedi as the head of state presiding over and framing the reform.","contrary_evidence":["The source is presidential and self-justifying, so independent corroboration would strengthen the claim."],"lenses":["4B.4","4B.5"]}

Search ledger:
- Candidates found this wave: about 20.
- Documents opened this wave: 11.
- Duplicate families rejected: 5.
- Irrelevant or out-of-period items rejected: 3.
- Inaccessible items: 2.
- Accepted distinct URLs this wave: 9.
- Accepted distinct URLs cumulative across all waves: 39.
- Distinct domains cumulative across all waves: at least 15.

Material gaps:
- Direct 2022 evidence of ruler-level election-rule manipulation remains thinner than the broader institutional distrust record.
- Direct evidence on surveillance, internet shutdowns, or digital controls by Tshisekedi remains sparse.
- Direct evidence on term-limit pressure and succession maneuvering is still mostly inferential from process warnings and public pledges.
- Evidence on women, opposition regions, and unpopular viewpoints is still thinner than the press and election-process record.

